      {
        "id": 86330,
        "name": "NAL0781",
        "username": "NAL0781",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/nal0781/{size}/2041_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-15T01:10:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Envisioner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Envisioner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If Parse targets weak points, I hope that she does irreducible damage.I'm hoping that KNYFE will have some cards that aren't just More Stabby-Dakka, but also some stuff representing her espionage and intelligence side.&nbsp; Like how Trust Fund doesn't seem to match the rest of Wraith's deck, but is integral in getting her the many tools she chooses among.&nbsp; I'm hoping KNYFE is a bit of a scout and agent, as well as a damage-dealer.&nbsp; She should have some effect that gives her the equivalent of Wraith's Stealth ability, though her innate Power is probably more like F6 Wraith's Last Stand ability.&nbsp; Perhaps it could be \"KNYFE deals 1 melee damage to any target.&nbsp; KNYFE deals 1 melee damage to any target.\"&nbsp; That way, it'd be similar to Fanatic, minus the two different damage types, but plus the flexibility to hit the same target or different targets, as with O-X's Rocket Punch.For Natch, since we already have Bunker's Modes, Mr. Fixer's Styles and Tools, and Scholar's Elementals, I'm hoping for something a little different.&nbsp; My theory?&nbsp; His deck consists of a lot of one-shots which have one basic effect (perhaps just drawing some cards, or dealing a little damage, and another effect depending on which form he's in.&nbsp; For example:<strong>Antelope Alertness</strong> - Ongoing.&nbsp; At the start of your turn, draw a card.&nbsp; At the end of your turn, if The Naturalist is in Gazelle Form, draw a card.<strong>Crocodile's Jaws</strong> - One-Shot.&nbsp; The Naturalist deals 3/4 melee damage to any target.&nbsp; If The Naturalist is in Crocodile Form, a target damaged this way cannot deal damage until the start of The Naturalist's turn.<strong>Rhino Charge</strong> - One-Shot.&nbsp; If The Naturalist is in Rhino Form, he deals 5 melee damage to any target.&nbsp; Draw five cards, then discard three cards.<strong>Herd Instinct</strong> - One-Shot.&nbsp; Reduce the next damage dealt to The Naturalist by 2.&nbsp; If The Naturalist is in Gazelle Form, reduce all damage dealt to him by 1 until the start of his next turn.&nbsp; Draw a card.<strong>Bloody Horns</strong> - Ongoing.&nbsp; Increase damage dealt to The Naturalist by 1.&nbsp; If The Naturalist is in Rhino Form, increase damage dealt by the Naturalist by 2.&nbsp; If The Naturalist is in Gazelle Form, whenever The Naturalist would deal damage to a target, instead he deals that much damage to all non-hero targets.<strong>River Lurker</strong> - Ongoing.&nbsp; The Naturalist is immune to damage from environment cards.&nbsp; If The Naturalist is in Crocodile Form, draw a card whenever an environment card is destroyed.&nbsp; If The Naturalist is in Gazelle Form, redirect all damage dealt to hero targets by Environment cards to The Naturalist.(For some reason, I really seem to like Gazelle form.)Setback and the Sentinels I have no real clue on.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Love these ideas.&nbsp; I don't have quite the imagination to come up with this level of detail (and that's why I'm a consumer and not a producer), but appreciate those that can put the thought in it.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
